    "Courses at Faculty of Technology | UTB\nCourses at Faculty of Technology | UTB\nCourses\nUpcoming\nImportant dates\n03\nNov\nevent\nBusiness Day 2026\n06\nNov\ntbu\nOpen Day at TBU\n06\nNov\ntbu\nOpen Day at TBU\nCalendar\nFacebook\nInstagram\nTwitter\nYoutube\nCourses at Faculty of Technology\nLevel of offered courses\nInternational students are allowed to choose freely which courses to take – possible recommendations/restrictions noted in column Note(s). Bachelor students are allowed to take master’s courses and the other way around, so the column Degree programme states the level of the course and its difficulty. Master’s courses should be more complicated, and the requirements might be higher.\nSemester of study\nEach course is defined in which semester it will be taught. It could be either in the\nWinter\nor\nSummer\nsemester. It cannot be changed. Nevertheless, some courses are offered in\nBoth\nsemesters.\nCredit requirements\nThe\nrequired minimum\nnumber of selected credits is\n15 ECTS\nper academic semester. The maximum number is not defined, but we recommend 30 ECTS credits as the maximum.\nMedium of instruction\nThe medium of instruction for courses offered below is\nEnglish\n, unless otherwise stated.\nList of courses for international exchange students\nAcademic year 2026/2027 (last update on 02/06/2026)\nCourse code (abbreviation)\nCourse name\nLecturer\nDegree programme\nECTS credits\nSemester\nNote(s)\nDepartment of Polymer Engineering (TUIP)\nTEDP\nMaster Thesis\nMaster\n30\nBoth\nThe TBU supervisor must agree with the thesis topic in advance and agree with the supervising of the student.\nTE5ZT\nPolymer Processing Engineering\ndoc. Ing. Martina Hřibová, Ph.D.\nBachelor\n4\nWinter\nTE5PR\nProcess Engineering II\nprof. Ing. Petr Svoboda, Ph.D.\nBachelor\n7\nWinter\nTE9PM\nAdvanced  Materials and Technologies\nprof. Ing. Tomáš Sedláček, Ph.D.\nMaster\n5\nWinter\nPrerequisite: knowledge of macromolecular chemistry from a Bachelor’s level.\nTE7AR\